  partName: Sensor (7)
  description: The Sensor (7) is a tiny, complex device situated at the top-center-rear
    of the engine, constructed from Material.001, responsible for monitoring and
    reporting critical engine parameters, such as oil pressure and temperature, which
    is essential for optimal engine performance and efficiency. Its complex shape
    allows for precise measurements and its rear position enables it to capture data
    from the engine's cooling system. Notably, the Sensor (7) is designed to provide
    real-time data, enabling the engine control unit to make adjustments for optimal
    performance.
